Use `sagedoc` to inspect documentation for
public names exported by `sage.all`.

Set `SAGEDOC_PYTHON` to the Python executable
inside the intended Sage environment. The command
never guesses an interpreter from `PATH`.

A whitespace-free query is an exact,
case-sensitive name lookup, for example `sagedoc GF`
or `sagedoc AffineGroup`.

A query containing whitespace is a ranked documentation
search, for example `sagedoc finite field construction`.

Results are JSON `indexing.Envelope` values. Exact hits
contain complete docstrings; searches contain snippets.
Add `-v` only when ranking scores are useful.

The index covers documented public `sage.all` exports,
not methods or every source declaration. Use the configured
Sage interpreter directly—typically `$SAGEDOC_PYTHON -c '...'`
to inspect methods, source, or APIs outside `sage.all`.
